fields.§h:Description:
While landing ~30 runs, the human had to approve around 100 Bash permission prompts from the overseer, nearly all of them read-only (git show/log/diff, grep, ls, cat) or routine git work inside ~/.dispatch/worktrees/<project>/<run> (rebase, worktree add). That is slow and pointless.

Done looks like:
- When dispatch launches the overseer Claude Code session, it passes a permission profile (via --settings / --allowedTools or a generated settings file, NOT by having the agent edit its own settings) that:
  - adds ~/.dispatch/worktrees as an additional directory, so cd/Read/Edit there are not treated as outside the project;
  - allows read-only shell (git show/log/diff/status/branch, ls, cat, head, tail, grep, rg, find, sed -n, wc, jq) and the read-only overseer MCP tools without a prompt;
  - allows routine git in run worktrees (fetch, rebase, worktree add, commit) and moon verify tasks;
  - still prompts or denies destructive ones: push --force, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, worktree remove, anything writing under .dispatch/.
- A setting in the desktop app to choose strict vs. this default profile.
- Tests that the generated profile contains the expected allow/deny rules.
